ination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-20508/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20508"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection/97d9f21ba3a563f740146a2ded05ef7b7b7771fc829af56f11b56abaae794c5c" :answer/id #uuid "e0cfebc0-40c3-5725-b157-1599893c16b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection/2cf629bc1e3ef5afd0a0e557b01ef0433f30be0665cbfe0ddc184cb86e561332" :answer/id #uuid "94e9bcbb-a440-5237-9d40-d9b7887bbeda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection/1ad518518e403f415fdddc64117f0051e163aed6117756339f730321fb0d614c" :answer/id #uuid "27e46dfc-95ae-5910-96da-2cb4e55ebddd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection/1f0b1f31567997d8e9d359989149aecbca05057bf0e7cf6aaa2f005add31011f" :answer/id #uuid "64e2d1b5-6836-5533-bb22-8b5655bae736" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection/1055be64d5cef005df193d5c454d7357ba445a16d6f6986823bdc1f55655ff4b" :answer/id #uuid "d62a83a2-5949-5c80-b251-d8b57f98e411" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "36858ecf-b05d-5ee4-af71-6b15e5748fc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20542/selection/1ad518518e403f415fdddc64117f0051e163aed6117756339f730321fb0d614c" :answer-field/choices ["q-20542/selection/97d9f21ba3a563f740146a2ded05ef7b7b7771fc829af56f11b56abaae794c5c" "q-20542/selection/2cf629bc1e3ef5afd0a0e557b01ef0433f30be0665cbfe0ddc184cb86e561332" "q-20542/selection/1ad518518e403f415fdddc64117f0051e163aed6117756339f730321fb0d614c" "q-20542/selection/1f0b1f31567997d8e9d359989149aecbca05057bf0e7cf6aaa2f005add31011f" "q-20542/selection/1055be64d5cef005df193d5c454d7357ba445a16d6f6986823bdc1f55655ff4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20542" :question/id #uuid "41dc60ae-16df-5d77-80b8-f746d03ba119" :question/math-academy-id "q-20542" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & x+2y+2z=2 \\\\  & 3x+4y+4z=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y=5 \\\\  & z=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection/34218b32df20b1bbbc00084edc6b5bab194156620c44cf001f1c669e22985158" :answer/id #uuid "8100d4e5-8239-55c1-82b3-13ffcad4aded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection/2a73f5b041c84013f91b4cf15c4fc17546f04dcd56d161cd19741ddb2725e24c" :answer/id #uuid "24e6fed1-476a-5e48-b079-1921ac3039cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection/7441c86bea977924323fd07c83ca3f63b8c1d215081a137f4f1acca70e17be3e" :answer/id #uuid "70e05e5f-0032-5342-aeb4-8241faa7b956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection/70a5c9bc4f179d7298d5291b4d4dcfb97af5f7e1f0503aff20adb8eae60c6e9e" :answer/id #uuid "4c6e9ba9-4b7d-56e2-a453-f40b03ee0519" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection/93d8936a4600f4945fb7565a5f01bbe95af66085cdb14b403b8bddde6c950c86" :answer/id #uuid "1309a08f-7d67-5c97-899e-7bf10126abcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf4cf26-97d2-516e-84fd-52fee47d4cbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73580/selection/7441c86bea977924323fd07c83ca3f63b8c1d215081a137f4f1acca70e17be3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-73580/selection/34218b32df20b1bbbc00084edc6b5bab194156620c44cf001f1c669e22985158" "q-73580/selection/2a73f5b041c84013f91b4cf15c4fc17546f04dcd56d161cd19741ddb2725e24c" "q-73580/selection/7441c86bea977924323fd07c83ca3f63b8c1d215081a137f4f1acca70e17be3e" "q-73580/selection/70a5c9bc4f179d7298d5291b4d4dcfb97af5f7e1f0503aff20adb8eae60c6e9e" "q-73580/selection/93d8936a4600f4945fb7565a5f01bbe95af66085cdb14b403b8bddde6c950c86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73580" :question/id #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" :question/math-academy-id "q-73580" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73580/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection/1a111f0e2762b318594304536c8a439917c59d55113c50d4537f8cd530d8a705" :answer/id #uuid "6b06bdab-8dde-5ae4-82b6-bdd85432ec26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection/bfb16e3fb6506b9352896866f73e2ab272b2b3829c2f0b39067f9801b7a4da28" :answer/id #uuid "2d98a077-0d09-5c3c-a4d2-a14130b0985f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection/b2124b149c5768e6c3117b9a703de1fc4d1255b43a1367d133508a7ceb029b17" :answer/id #uuid "cf67d0ad-a5bc-5246-a10c-473e813e4bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection/6824ad512d50589c3810216ec46968d1e1b7e570d544cd310dce1201cd755700" :answer/id #uuid "c09a3337-5bdd-5b70-afda-6a915f809f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection/7b92a9309d37eb5de5a909137c13df0fd20b95ae5e347757d44405c508e8453d" :answer/id #uuid "a0fb858d-7410-530c-a535-374f4bf7db06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f992923-2287-5ec0-ad19-e08e3601aa2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73579/selection/1a111f0e2762b318594304536c8a439917c59d55113c50d4537f8cd530d8a705" :answer-field/choices ["q-73579/selection/1a111f0e2762b318594304536c8a439917c59d55113c50d4537f8cd530d8a705" "q-73579/selection/bfb16e3fb6506b9352896866f73e2ab272b2b3829c2f0b39067f9801b7a4da28" "q-73579/selection/b2124b149c5768e6c3117b9a703de1fc4d1255b43a1367d133508a7ceb029b17" "q-73579/selection/6824ad512d50589c3810216ec46968d1e1b7e570d544cd310dce1201cd755700" "q-73579/selection/7b92a9309d37eb5de5a909137c13df0fd20b95ae5e347757d44405c508e8453d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73579" :question/id #uuid "20ff081a-4610-5c30-9be5-fa40ee345274" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -3x+6y-3z=18 \\\\  & -4x+8y-3z=2 \\\\  & y-4z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z=-6 \\\\ y-4z=-3 \\\\ z=-22,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22)=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22)=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73579/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection/7750224d77e091b39eb90053a041d20a2351469311d9b2e19e076b98a7b12e6c" :answer/id #uuid "3f210db8-3b25-5f8e-8b04-4326d3813eaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection/620d189562ba99617557ff881d63821d17e956faf7c756c608256d230803f746" :answer/id #uuid "7a77cf3d-adf9-549d-960c-c60db24c45dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection/ec62b406b72ee955c67a7ca83368dbd8b786e751c28a21f26f2e7ce01ea5c628" :answer/id #uuid "1b2ad833-e3f0-5fe8-9a5e-bce6a9cadabc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection/44d9a37693dd25c9e84fdec8439545d00fc58e1b46c3d50467e9f6b29cd6ebf1" :answer/id #uuid "237aa6f1-4bcf-54d7-a265-35842fd96b97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection/610f948a085e848991999d1fd04891b894d0934e2137f20d65b5b239ed72e98c" :answer/id #uuid "a9b32cd9-62b8-5cda-8c27-344ecb042797" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27ead658-1607-5e21-bef8-9859ed283c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130927/selection/610f948a085e848991999d1fd04891b894d0934e2137f20d65b5b239ed72e98c" :answer-field/choices ["q-130927/selection/7750224d77e091b39eb90053a041d20a2351469311d9b2e19e076b98a7b12e6c" "q-130927/selection/620d189562ba99617557ff881d63821d17e956faf7c756c608256d230803f746" "q-130927/selection/ec62b406b72ee955c67a7ca83368dbd8b786e751c28a21f26f2e7ce01ea5c628" "q-130927/selection/44d9a37693dd25c9e84fdec8439545d00fc58e1b46c3d50467e9f6b29cd6ebf1" "q-130927/selection/610f948a085e848991999d1fd04891b894d0934e2137f20d65b5b239ed72e98c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130927" :question/id #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" :question/math-academy-id "q-130927" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=4 \\\\ y+2z=-2 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4)=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130927/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73396"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection/c7d74c302fa695766920f092f29fcc43053e382c5afc331f596bdfa850b39cf7" :answer/id #uuid "c6ec3980-8f7f-5956-9395-d25572148fdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection/104ec8fcf201545e4422cdf2ebfb375e071a9fb90bc4348d71408a4abc2a0999" :answer/id #uuid "24bf5c93-01a8-5636-94b1-c4ee5dc208b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection/17756f1170a4bd769dbbc59eb7df0429b3ec2297c5ee0494c9b090d713b0a8c8" :answer/id #uuid "fdbf2bac-e66d-5284-aee3-3749274a9cbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection/0415fff138ba19605b98c2f416f8f6e8b6820d228d34821a2fdc72a23a022559" :answer/id #uuid "1b44ac0b-f0a6-5169-91fa-ccd943551ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection/3ef9a8d941d7c9c64b4e307f9cb61220919d82e5fb4d349168d31e88b9509ba4" :answer/id #uuid "f9d5d5c5-0faa-553d-8841-fbb325465107" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e845c512-1717-5897-a5f6-26fcd9cc631e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73584/selection/17756f1170a4bd769dbbc59eb7df0429b3ec2297c5ee0494c9b090d713b0a8c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-73584/selection/c7d74c302fa695766920f092f29fcc43053e382c5afc331f596bdfa850b39cf7" "q-73584/selection/104ec8fcf201545e4422cdf2ebfb375e071a9fb90bc4348d71408a4abc2a0999" "q-73584/selection/17756f1170a4bd769dbbc59eb7df0429b3ec2297c5ee0494c9b090d713b0a8c8" "q-73584/selection/0415fff138ba19605b98c2f416f8f6e8b6820d228d34821a2fdc72a23a022559" "q-73584/selection/3ef9a8d941d7c9c64b4e307f9cb61220919d82e5fb4d349168d31e88b9509ba4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73584" :question/id #uuid "2165c009-aa54-51cd-9ee0-62e80fd9ad16" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z=3 \\\\ y+5z=-8 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4)=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4)=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73584/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4701"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ z=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4702"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=-2 \\\\  & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & x+2y+z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=-2 \\\\ y=3 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
